    "tpc_seq": 1,
    "tpc_book": "<div><strong>International Finance (2025F-Master Program)</strong></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><strong>Reading List</strong></div>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li><strong>Introduction</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n<div>Basic Concepts: National Income Accounting, Balance of Payment Accounting, Balance Sheet of Central Bank, and Definitions of Exchange Rate (Lecture Notes)</div>\n\n<div>Lane, Philip R and Gian Maria Milesi-Ferretti (2007), &ldquo;The External Wealth of Nations Mark II: Revised and Extended Estimates of Foreign Assets and Liabilities, 1970&ndash;2004,&rdquo; <em>Journal of International Economics</em>, 73(2): 223-250.</div>\n\n<div>Ethan Ilzetzki Carmen M. Reinhart Kenneth S. Rogoff (2017), &ldquo;Exchange Arrangements Entering the 21st Century: Which Anchor will Hold?&rdquo; <em>IMF Working Paper</em>, No. 23134.</div>\n\n<div>IMF (2023), &ldquo;Annual Report on Exchange Arrangement and Exchange Restrictions: Overview 2022,&rdquo; International Monetary Fund.</div>\n\n<div>Reserve Bank of Australia (2024), Exchange Rates and their Measurement, <a href=\"https://www.rba.gov.au/education/resources/explainers/exchange-rates-and-their-measurement.html\">https://www.rba.gov.au/education/resources/explainers/exchange-rates-and-their-measurement.html</a>. Reserve Bank of Australia: https://www.rba.gov.au/education/resources/</div>\n\n<div>楊政郎、簡仲德、顏厚棟 (2010), &ldquo;台灣最適外匯準備持有量之評估&rdquo;，經濟論文，Vol. 38, No. 4, 579-618.</div>\n\n<div>Koepke, R. (2019), &quot;What Drives Capital Flows to Emerging Markets? A Survey of The Empirical Literature,&quot; Journal of Economic Surveys, Vol. 33, No. 2, 516-540.</div>\n\n<div>陳虹宇, 吳聰敏, 李怡庭, 陳旭昇 (2021)，致富的特權：二十年來我們為央行政策付出的代價，春山出版 。</div>\n\n<div>Economist (2025), &ldquo;A New Financial Order,&rdquo; Special Report, May 31.</div>\n\n<div>Economist (2025), &ldquo;Our Big Mac index will sadden America&rsquo;s burger-lovers,&rdquo; July 16.</div>\n\n<div>Bowman, M.W. (2024), &ldquo;The Federal Reserve&rsquo;s Balance Sheet as a Monetary Policy Tool: Past Lessons and Future Considerations,&rdquo; 2024 BOJ-IMES Conference, hosted by the Institute for Monetary and Economic Studies, Bank of Japan.</div>\n\n<div><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 2. Current Account: sustainability, adjustment, and determinants </strong></div>\n\n<div>Freund, C. L. (2000), &ldquo;Current Account Adjustment in Industrialized Countries,&rdquo;<em> Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System</em>, International Finance Discussion Papers, No. 692.</div>\n\n<div>Chinn, Menzie and Eswar Prasad (2003), &ldquo;Medium-Term Determinants of Current Accounts in Industrial and Developing Countries: An Empirical Exploration,&rdquo; <em>Journal of International Economics</em>, 59, 47-76.</div>\n\n<div>Obstfeld, M. (1995), &ldquo;Chapter 34 The intertemporal approach to the current account,&rdquo; Handbook of International Economics, <a href=\"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/journal/15734404/3/supp/C\">Volume 3</a>, 1731-1799, Elsevier.</div>\n\n<div>Yan, Ho-don (2007), &ldquo;Does Capital Mobility Finance or Cause a Current Account Imbalance?,&rdquo;<em> Quarterly Review of Economics and Finance</em>, Vol. 47, 1-25.</div>\n\n<div>Koepke, R. (2019), &quot;What Drives Capital Flows to Emerging Markets? A Survey of The Empirical Literature,&quot; <em>Journal of Economic Surveys</em>, Vol. 33, No. 2, 516-540.</div>\n\n<div><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;3. Exchange Rate: &nbsp;Determination, Misalignment, and Exchange Rate Regime,</strong></div>\n\n<div><a name=\"_Hlk175239391\">陳旭昇</a>與吳聰敏 (2008), &quot;台灣匯率制度初探,&quot; 《經濟論文叢刊》 [&quot;An Investigation of Exchange Rate Policy in Taiwan,&quot; Taiwan Economic Review], 36:2, 147-182.</div>\n\n<div>Rodrik, Dani (2008), &ldquo;The Real Exchange Rate and Economic Growth.&rdquo; <em>Brookings Papers on Economic Activity </em>2.</div>\n\n<div>Levy-Yeyati, Eduardo, and Federico Sturzenegger (2007), &ldquo;Fear of Appreciation,&rdquo; <em>Policy Research Working Paper Series</em> 4387.</div>\n\n<div>陳旭昇 (2022), &quot;新台幣匯率與貿易條件惡化,&quot;《經濟論文叢刊》 &quot;Terms of Trade Deterioration and Exchange Rates: The Case of Taiwan&quot; Taiwan Economic Review], 50:1, 51-85.</div>\n\n<div>Yan, Ho-Don and Cheng-lang Yang (2012), &ldquo;Does An Undervalued Currency Merit Economic Growth &ndash; Evidence from Taiwan,&rdquo; Panoeconomicus, Vol. 59, Issue 1, pp. 37-57.</div>\n\n<div><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 4.</strong> <strong>Financial Globalization: Causes, Consequences, and Policy Response</strong></div>\n\n<div>Fratzscher, M (2011), &ldquo;Capital Flows, Push versus Pull Factors and the Global Financial Crisis,&rdquo; NBER Working Paper 17357.</div>\n\n<div>*Feldstein, M. and C. Horioka (1980), &ldquo;Domestic Saving and International Capital Flows,&rdquo; Economic Journal, 90 (358): 314&ndash;329.</div>\n\n<div>Taylor, A.M. (1996), &ldquo;International Capital Mobility in History: The Saving-Investment Relationship,&rdquo; NBER Working Paper No. 5743.</div>\n\n<div>*Forbes, K.J. and F.E. Warnock (2012), &ldquo;Capital Flow Waves: Surge, Stops, Flight, and Retrenchment,&rdquo; <em>Journal of International Economics</em>, 88(2): 235-251.</div>\n\n<div>*Cardarelli, R., S. Elekdag, and M.A. Kose (2010), &ldquo;Capital Inflows: Macroeconomic Implications and Policy Responses,&rdquo; <em>Economic System</em>, 34, 333-356.</div>\n\n<div>*Hahm, J.-H., F.S. Mishkin, H. S. Shin, and K. Shin (2012), &ldquo;Macroprudential Policies in Open Emerging Economies,&rdquo; <em>NBER Working Paper</em>, No. 17780.</div>\n\n<div>*Ostry, J., A.R. Ghosh, M. Chamon, and M.S. Qureshi (2011), &ldquo;Capital Controls: When and Why?&rdquo; <em>IMF Economic Review</em>, Vol. 59, No. 3, 562-580.</div>\n\n<div>L&oacute;pez, G.G. and L. Stracca (2021), &ldquo;Changing patterns of capital flows,&rdquo; CGFS Papers No. 66, Bank for International Settlements.</div>\n\n<div><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 5. </strong><strong>Financial Crises: Types, causes, and policy responses</strong></div>\n\n<div>*Aliber, R.Z. and C.P. Kindleberger (2015), <em>Manias, Panics, and Crashes &ndash; A History of Financial Crisis</em>, Chapter 2: The Anatomy of a Typical Crisis, 7th edition, Palgrave Macmillan, 38-52.</div>\n\n<div>Milesi-Ferretti, Gian Maria and Assaf Razin (1998), &ldquo;Current Account Reversals and Currency Crises: Empirical Regularities,&rdquo; CEPR Discussion Paper, No. 1921, or NBER Working Paper, No. 6620, and in P. Krugman (2000) (ed.) <em>Currency Crises</em>, U. of Chicago Press.</div>\n\n<div>*Blanchard, O. (2009), &ldquo;The Crisis: Basic Mechanisms, and Appropriate Policies,&rdquo; <em>IMF Working Paper</em>, WP/09/80.</div>\n\n<div>Reinhart, C. and K. Rogoff (2012), &ldquo;<a href=\"https://ideas.repec.org/p/pra/mprapa/51258.html\">Causes of Financial Crises Past and Present: The Role of the This Time is Different Syndrome</a>,&rdquo;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://ideas.repec.org/s/pra/mprapa.html\"><em>MPRA Paper</em></a><em>&nbsp;</em><em>51258</em>, University Library of Munich, Germany.</div>\n\n<div>Obstfeld, M. (2012), &ldquo;Financial Flows, Financial Crises, and Global Imbalances,&quot; <em>Journal of International Money and Finance</em>, 31, 469-480.</div>\n\n<div>Lane, P. (2012), &ldquo;Financial Globalization and Crises,&rdquo; <em>BIS Working Papers</em>, No. 397.</div>\n",
    "tpc_book_en": null
  },
